# Stale reference 2 — storage-description rdfs:seeAlso points at the retired
# wiki/sources/ container. D98 merged sources INTO concepts (not a rename to a
# sibling): the Type Index routes BOTH skos:Concept and wiki:Source to
# wiki/concepts/. So this seeAlso entry has no distinct live replacement — it
# is subsumed by the concepts/ entry and should be removed, not repointed.
<urn:uuid:a4458e72-1dee-417c-8c16-f1a478b77849>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/settings/publicTypeIndex> ;   # ground truth: forClass wiki:Source -> wiki/concepts/
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:SupersededConcept ;
    mem:rationale "Storage description rdfs:seeAlso lists <../wiki/sources/>, which returns 404. Unlike pages (a 1:1 rename to concepts), D98 MERGED sources into concepts: the Type Index publicTypeIndex routes both skos:Concept and wiki:Source to instanceContainer <../wiki/concepts/>. There is no surviving wiki/sources/ container to repoint to. Classified SupersededConcept (a decision retired the named container by absorbing it) rather than a plain DanglingReference, because the correct repair is removal of the redundant pointer, with the concepts/ seeAlso (added in proposal 01) already covering both content kinds. wiki:Source itself is preserved as a class via the class-extension contract; only the separate container pointer is stale. Resolved against the Type Index (operational truth). Repair direction: pointer -> reality. Lives in the STATIC css/config/void-description.json -> repo edit." ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:16:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

